schema: "0.3"
id: echo-of-manifestation-creature-drowned-hawker
type: image
service: gemini

prompt:
  text: >
    Dark fantasy concept art of a Drowned Hawker — an ambient enemy found in Zone 2,
    the Sunken Market. A drowned merchant standing waist-deep in the shadow-water of the
    flooded bazaar. The figure wears waterlogged merchant's clothing — a heavy coat, an
    apron with many pockets — swollen with absorbed shadow-water, the fabric darkened and
    heavy. Its most disturbing feature is the mouth: it opens impossibly wide, far beyond
    human jaw capacity, as if trying to swallow something larger than itself, the lips
    stretched thin and the throat visible as a dark tunnel. Goods that once belonged to the
    merchant's stall orbit slowly around its body in the shadow-water — brass pots, spice
    tins, cloth bolts, lanterns — circling like satellites, pulled by the creature's
    residual merchant-need to hold its wares. The hawker's hands are raised slightly, palms
    up, in a perpetual offering gesture, but the items it offers are its orbiting debris.
    Its eyes are clouded and unfocused, the look of someone who drowned while trying to
    save their inventory. Bioluminescent teal light from the shadow-water illuminates the
    creature from below, casting its swollen features in sickly underlighting. Background
    shows the Sunken Market — flooded stalls, teal glow, tarnished copper. Painterly style,
    the mood is commerce corrupted into compulsive offering of worthless goods.
  negative: "bright, cheerful, cartoon, anime, clean magic, zombie, generic drowned body, simple monster, colorful palette, bright teal, clean water, low detail, flat shading, pirate"

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1024
    height: 1536
    aspect_ratio: "2:3"

tags: [creature, ambient-enemy, zone-2, drowned, merchant, market, concept-art, dark-fantasy]
